From: SJ Park <sj@kernel.org>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 13:48:23 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] mm/damon/api: define damon_report data structure

Define a struct for data attribute report.  DAMON's data attribute
report API callers can format their report using it.  The struct
provides public fields for the type and the memory address range.  The
type field represents the reporting data attribute type.  The address
range is for the memory of the reporting attribute.  It also provides a
private field for recording when the report is submitted.

Note that currently no real report type exists.  This is a place holder.

Signed-off-by: SJ Park <sj@kernel.org>
---
 include/linux/damon.h | 23 +++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 23 insertions(+)

diff --git a/include/linux/damon.h b/include/linux/damon.h
index 06bd92981af21..5c32ddebf4625 100644
--- a/include/linux/damon.h
+++ b/include/linux/damon.h
@@ -751,6 +751,29 @@ struct damon_intervals_goal {
 	unsigned long max_sample_us;
 };
 
+/**
+ * enum damon_report_type - Type of &struct damon_report.
+ */
+enum damon_report_type {
+	NR_DAMON_REPORT_TYPES,
+};
+
+/**
+ * struct damon_report - Data attribute report information.
+ *
+ * @type:	Type of the report.
+ * @addr_range:	The address range of the memory to report for.
+ *
+ * Note that the @start_addr and @end_adr represents an end-open range.
+ */
+struct damon_report {
+	enum damon_report_type type;
+	struct damon_addr_range addr_range;
+/* private: */
+	/* when this report is generated */
+	unsigned long jiffies;
+};
+
 /**
  * enum damon_prep_action - DAMON probing preparation action.
  *
-- 
